---
// QuickStart.astro
---

<section id="quickstart" class="py-20 max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
  <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-16 space-y-4">
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-brand-500/10 text-brand-500 border border-brand-500/20">
      Quick Start
    </div>
    <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
      Up and Running in 30 Seconds
    </h2>
    <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
      Three simple steps to install the toolchain, write your first script, and run it at sub-millisecond speeds.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
    
    <!-- Step 1: Install -->
    <div class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-[#0D121C] border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-6 shadow-sm relative">
      <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-500 text-white font-bold flex items-center justify-center text-sm mb-4 shadow-md shadow-brand-500/20">
        1
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
        Install with Homebrew
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Install the official standalone RHP binary for macOS or Linux using Homebrew.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-auto rounded-xl bg-slate-950 p-3.5 border border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs text-slate-200 overflow-x-auto">
        <span class="text-brand-500">$</span> brew install vuenice/rhp/rhp
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 2: Write Code -->
    <div class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-[#0D121C] border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-6 shadow-sm relative">
      <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-500 text-white font-bold flex items-center justify-center text-sm mb-4 shadow-md shadow-brand-500/20">
        2
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
        Write hello.rhp
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Write clean PHP-style syntax utilizing Rust-backed static facades like <code class="text-brand-400 font-mono">Str</code> and <code class="text-brand-400 font-mono">Sys</code>.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-auto rounded-xl bg-slate-950 p-3.5 border border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs text-slate-200 overflow-x-auto">
        <pre><code><span class="text-brand-400">string</span> <span class="text-cyan-300">$slug</span> = <span class="text-amber-300">Str::slug</span>(<span class="text-emerald-300">"Hello RHP"</span>);
<span class="text-amber-300">print</span>(<span class="text-cyan-300">$slug</span>);</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 3: Run -->
    <div class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-[#0D121C] border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-6 shadow-sm relative">
      <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-500 text-white font-bold flex items-center justify-center text-sm mb-4 shadow-md shadow-brand-500/20">
        3
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
        Execute with rhp CLI
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Run instantly with the AST development interpreter, or compile to bytecode VM via production mode.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-auto rounded-xl bg-slate-950 p-3.5 border border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs text-slate-200 overflow-x-auto">
        <div class="text-slate-400"># Dev mode (auto-picks index.rhp)</div>
        <div><span class="text-brand-500">$</span> rhp run dev</div>
        <div class="text-slate-400 mt-1"># Or explicit file</div>
        <div><span class="text-brand-500">$</span> rhp run dev --file="hello.rhp"</div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
